  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "We then, as workers together with him, beseech you also that ye receive not the grace of God in vain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "(For he saith, I have heard thee in a time accepted, and in the day of salvation have I succoured thee: behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation.)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Giving no offence in any thing, that the ministry be not blamed:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But in all things approving ourselves as the ministers of God, in much patience, in afflictions, in necessities, in distresses,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "In stripes, in imprisonments, in tumults, in labours, in watchings, in fastings;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "By pureness, by knowledge, by longsuffering, by kindness, by the Holy Ghost, by love unfeigned,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "By the word of truth, by the power of God, by the armour of righteousness on the right hand and on the left,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "By honour and dishonour, by evil report and good report: as deceivers, and yet true;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "As unknown, and yet well known; as dying, and, behold, we live; as chastened, and not killed;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "As sorrowful, yet alway rejoicing; as poor, yet making many rich; as having nothing, and yet possessing all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "O ye Corinthians, our mouth is open unto you, our heart is enlarged.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Ye are not straitened in us, but ye are straitened in your own bowels.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Now for a recompence in the same, (I speak as unto my children,) be ye also enlarged.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers: for what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness? and what communion hath light with darkness?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And what concord hath Christ with Belial? or what part hath he that believeth with an infidel?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And what agreement hath the temple of God with idols? for ye are the temple of the living God; as God hath said, I will dwell in them, and walk in them; and I will be their God, and they shall be my people.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith the Lord, and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And will be a Father unto you, and ye shall be my sons and daughters, saith the Lord Almighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 6:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-corinthians:6:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
